  <prompt>
    Delete the AnalysisWorkspace code page: the src/client/code-pages/AnalysisWorkspace/ source tree (incl. launcher/,
    src/, build-webresource.ps1), scripts/Deploy-AnalysisWorkspace.ps1, and the Dataverse web resources
    (sprk_analysisworkspace HTML, sprk_AnalysisWorkspaceLauncher JS) plus the dead custom page
    sprk_analysisworkspace_8bc0b in the environment. Reconcile the 4-name casing so nothing dangles. Shared-lib files that
    were extracted FROM AnalysisWorkspace (ThreePaneLayout, useTwoPanelLayout, SprkChatBridge, renderMarkdown,
    StreamingWriteHarness) are KEPT — do not delete them.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer + Dataverse deployer. Expert in code-page web-resource lifecycle and PAC-based web-resource
    deletion. Follow ADRs strictly; distinguish the retiring code page from the shared-lib components it seeded.
  </role>

  <goal>
    src/client/code-pages/AnalysisWorkspace/ + scripts/Deploy-AnalysisWorkspace.ps1 are deleted; the environment web
    resources (sprk_analysisworkspace, sprk_AnalysisWorkspaceLauncher) + dead custom page sprk_analysisworkspace_8bc0b are
    removed; the 4-name casing set has no dangling references; the kept shared-lib files still exist and build; a repo-wide
    Grep for analysisworkspace across C#/JS/solution returns zero (excluding trivial kept doc-comment mentions, which are
    also cleaned where trivial); build + deploy clean.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Per spec §13.5 / FR-21, once all deep-links + launch points are repointed (060,061) and the legacy session path is
